# A lambda is monomorphic.
#
# `id` is lambda-bound, so its parameter is one type that the uses
# settle between them -- the first call makes it Int and the second is
# refused. A `def` with the same body is polymorphic and serves both;
# that is the whole of the difference, and it is Hindley-Milner's own
# (PYKING.md, "Lambdas"; docs/type_inference.md).
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

def named(x): x

print(named(1), named("a"))

id = lam x. x

print(id(1))
print(id("a"))
